$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the Suzuki coupling on
the 3,9-diiodo-7H-benzo[ de]anthracen-7-one (19)
3,9-diiodo-7H-benzo[de]anthracen-7-one (19) (0.48 g, 1.0 mmol), aryl
boronic acid (2.5 mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (30 mg), PPh3 (20 mg), potassium
carbonate (1.38 g, 10.0 mmol) were taken in a mixture of toluene (50 ml)
and water (10 ml). Reaction mixture was heated at 110 ºC for 5 h in
nitrogen atmosphere. On completion of reaction, reaction mixture was
cooled and toluene layer was separated. Toluene was removed under vacuum,
and product was purified by column chromatography using
dichloromethane/hexane as eluent to afford product. Preparation of
3,9-diphenyl-7H-benzo[de]anthracen-7-one (20) According to general
reaction procedure, 3,9-diiodo-7H-benzo[de]anthracen-7-one (19) and
phenylboronic acid (0.26 g, 2.5 mmol) were reacted. Preparation of
7-(bis(4-fluorophenylphenyl)methylene)-7H-benzo[de]anthracene (16)
According to general reaction procedure,
7-(dichloromethylene)-7H-benzo[de]anthracene (13) (0.30 g, 1.0 mmol) and
(4-fluorophenyl)boronic acid (0.35 g, 2.5 mmol) were reacted. to give
product as yellow solid. Yield: 0.37 g, 88%. Mp: 245 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3,
400 MHz) δ: 8.16 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.95 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.79 (d,
J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.65-7.57 (m, 2H), 7.29-7.25 (m, 1H), 7.18-7.05 (m, 7H),
7.05-6.88 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ: 162.8, 160.3, 141.0,
139.8, 139.2, 134.6, 134.2, 133.8, 132.8, 132.2, 131.5, 131.4, 131.3,
131.1, 130.5, 128.5, 128.0, 127.4, 127.2, 126.8, 126.0, 125.0, 123.8,
119.8, 115.7, 115.5, 115.4, 115.2. MALDI-TOF MS: calculated for
[C30H18F2]+: 416.1371, found: 416.1379.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
