$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,4'-(2,5-Selenophenediyl)bispyridine-SeExBIPY 4-Pyridineboronic pinacol
ester (8.52 g, 41.5 mmol), 2,5-dibromoselenophene (5 g, 17.3 mmol),
Pd(PPh3)4 (2 g, 1.73 mmol) and K3PO4 (37 g, 155.8 mmol) were added to a
1:1 mixture of dry, degassed 1,4-dioxane:DMF (100 mL). The solution was
heated at 130°C under N2 for 72 h. The reaction mixture was then cooled
to room temperature and filtered. The organic phase was concentrated
under vacuum and the residue dissolved in CHCl3 and washed three times
with H2O. Concentrated HCl (ca. 1 mL) was then added to the organic
phase, resulting in precipitation of the product from solution. The
precipitate was collected by filtration and then dissolved in H2O.
Finally, aqueous NaOH (15 M) was added dropwise to the H2O layer until
the pH was ca. 8-9, which resulted in precipitation. Pure SeExBIPY (4.1
g, 14.4 mmol 83%) as a yellow solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz, (CD3)2SO) δ (ppm) =
8.60 (dd, 4H, J = 4.3 Hz, J = 1.7 Hz), 8.08 (2, 2H), 7.66 (dd, 4H, J =
4.3 Hz, J = 1.7 Hz); 13C NMR (126 MHz, (CD3)2SO) δ (ppm) = 150.6, 148.1,
141.9, 130.3, 120.0. ESI-MS: m/z = 287.0082 [SeExBIPY + H+]1+, 144.0077
[SeExBIPY + 2H+]2+; found, 287.0086 [SeExBIPY + H+]1+, 144.0082 [SeExBIPY
+ 2H+]2+.
